1
00:00:05,400 --> 00:00:07,280
The Beautification
Committee sure has it rough.

2
00:00:08,500 --> 00:00:10,970
It got this dirty in just one summer.

3
00:00:12,640 --> 00:00:14,480
It built up little by little.

4
00:00:16,380 --> 00:00:17,680
Just like us.

5
00:00:18,680 --> 00:00:20,620
Being compared to dirt...

6
00:00:20,720 --> 00:00:21,880
Hey.

7
00:00:24,390 --> 00:00:26,420
Summer break is over.

8
00:00:32,860 --> 00:00:34,400
Want to come over to my place?

9
00:00:36,770 --> 00:00:37,770
Huh...

10
00:00:41,500 --> 00:00:44,540
I don't want you to go home just yet today.

11
00:00:50,260 --> 00:00:54,350
Uh... well...

12
00:00:55,250 --> 00:00:56,290
Um...

13
00:01:02,490 --> 00:01:03,490
Sorry.

14
00:01:05,690 --> 00:01:07,130
I got ahead of myself.

15
00:01:08,020 --> 00:01:09,030
Huh?

16
00:01:10,380 --> 00:01:12,840
We shouldn't rush things like this.

17
00:01:16,040 --> 00:01:19,070
It's the first time we've spent
such a summery day together.

18
00:01:20,710 --> 00:01:23,350
Today was more than enough.

19
00:01:28,360 --> 00:01:30,420
Let's take it slow.

20
00:01:36,160 --> 00:01:37,160
Yeah...

21
00:01:47,720 --> 00:01:50,040
You never know who's watching at school.

22
00:01:51,540 --> 00:01:54,340
You never used to care about
that kind of thing, did you?

23
00:01:55,510 --> 00:01:57,480
Because we're dating now.

24
00:02:00,020 --> 00:02:01,020
- Huh?
- Sorry, sorry.

25
00:02:01,450 --> 00:02:02,520
What about cleaning?

26
00:02:04,890 --> 00:02:07,520
Would the pool really
be happy getting cleaned?

27
00:02:08,260 --> 00:02:09,260
Huh?

28
00:02:09,290 --> 00:02:11,790
Even though it just looks like dirt to us,

29
00:02:11,930 --> 00:02:14,890
it might actually be packed with a
whole summer's worth of memories, right?

30
00:02:16,700 --> 00:02:17,700
Whatever.

31
00:02:17,870 --> 00:02:19,430
Let's just take a break.

32
00:02:19,800 --> 00:02:21,200
Wanna play? Two-on-two.

33
00:02:21,440 --> 00:02:22,740
Uh... well...

34
00:02:23,940 --> 00:02:24,940
No.

35
00:02:25,340 --> 00:02:26,340
Let's play.

36
00:02:27,440 --> 00:02:28,456
Oh, didn't expect you to be so into it.

37
00:02:28,480 --> 00:02:29,480
Nice.

38
00:02:32,880 --> 00:02:34,420
I can take you on by myself.

39
00:02:34,680 --> 00:02:35,680
No.

40
00:02:36,050 --> 00:02:37,450
Count me in too.

41
00:02:44,240 --> 00:02:45,260
Alright.

42
00:02:45,430 --> 00:02:46,430
Bring it on.

43
00:02:47,230 --> 00:02:48,230
Nice one.

44
00:02:51,220 --> 00:02:52,220
I got it.

45
00:02:53,660 --> 00:02:54,660
Here you go.

46
00:02:59,720 --> 00:03:00,720
Oh.

47
00:03:00,900 --> 00:03:01,900
Excuse me.

48
00:03:02,340 --> 00:03:03,379
Komori-chan...

49
00:03:03,380 --> 00:03:05,480
What are you guys playing?

50
00:03:06,050 --> 00:03:08,520
Asamiya-kun, Tsunekawada-kun.

51
00:03:08,920 --> 00:03:11,050
You're not on the Beautification
Committee, are you?

52
00:03:13,690 --> 00:03:16,060
I'll put the ball away for you.

53
00:03:20,700 --> 00:03:22,700
Did she get nicer?

54
00:03:27,340 --> 00:03:29,040
Did something good happen?

55
00:03:29,670 --> 00:03:30,470
Huh?

56
00:03:30,470 --> 00:03:31,470
Over the summer break.

57
00:03:33,180 --> 00:03:34,980
Yeah, I guess.

58
00:03:36,550 --> 00:03:37,550
Asamiya.

59
00:03:37,780 --> 00:03:39,080
You're looking good.

60
00:03:52,590 --> 00:03:53,860
You're in love, aren't you?

61
00:03:54,100 --> 00:03:55,100
Huh?

62
00:03:55,130 --> 00:03:56,770
Eh, nothing's going on with me.

63
00:03:57,130 --> 00:03:58,370
No, I was talking about myself.

64
00:03:58,930 --> 00:04:00,970
Oh, you meant yourself.

65
00:04:01,640 --> 00:04:03,539
Huh? Who else would I mean?

66
00:04:03,540 --> 00:04:04,540
Never mind, never mind.

67
00:04:06,140 --> 00:04:07,810
So, what kind of person is it?

68
00:04:08,300 --> 00:04:11,259
It's a bit hard to explain.

69
00:04:11,260 --> 00:04:14,350
How should I put it? It's like I just
fell for them before I even realized it.

70
00:04:14,840 --> 00:04:17,090
Why did you want to tell me?

71
00:04:17,120 --> 00:04:19,400
Huh? Probably because I got carried away?

72
00:04:20,720 --> 00:04:23,360
When you like someone, don't
you just want to tell people about it?

73
00:04:25,130 --> 00:04:26,730
That's true.

74
00:04:39,210 --> 00:04:40,716
- Let's head back.
- Let's go, let's go.

75
00:04:40,740 --> 00:04:41,740
Let's go home.

76
00:04:43,620 --> 00:04:45,080
Good work today, everyone.

77
00:04:45,480 --> 00:04:47,419
Oh, I'm heading that way today too.

78
00:04:47,420 --> 00:04:48,420
Oh, really?

79
00:04:49,020 --> 00:04:50,320
- See you later.
- Bye.

80
00:04:51,720 --> 00:04:53,560
Actually, I'm getting carried away too.

81
00:04:54,590 --> 00:04:59,060
Dating Asamiya makes every day so much fun.

82
00:05:00,800 --> 00:05:01,860
But...

83
00:05:05,700 --> 00:05:06,739
Never mind.

84
00:05:06,740 --> 00:05:08,020
There's no one else around here.

85
00:05:09,840 --> 00:05:10,640
Yeah...

86
00:05:10,641 --> 00:05:14,980
Can we really keep
hiding this forever...?

87
00:05:59,400 --> 00:06:05,700
"After Moving Seats, The Boy Behind Me Has A Crush On Me"
(Episode 8)

88
00:06:11,370 --> 00:06:16,240
Can't we tell Sakaki and
the others... about us?

89
00:06:17,110 --> 00:06:17,970
Huh?

90
00:06:17,990 --> 00:06:20,710
I mean, we're all such good friends.

91
00:06:20,880 --> 00:06:21,939
If we keep keeping it a secret from them...

92
00:06:21,940 --> 00:06:23,420
It's better if we don't say anything.

93
00:06:27,580 --> 00:06:30,990
If you like how things are now,
then we definitely shouldn't tell them.

94
00:06:37,830 --> 00:06:40,930
Asamiya, do you really think this is okay?

95
00:06:44,310 --> 00:06:48,100
If it ends up with you getting hurt,

96
00:06:51,870 --> 00:06:53,580
that's the last thing I want to see.

97
00:07:06,590 --> 00:07:07,690
Let's go back.

98
00:07:11,330 --> 00:07:12,330
Yeah.

99
00:07:26,280 --> 00:07:27,540
Something on your mind?

100
00:07:28,570 --> 00:07:29,570
Huh?

101
00:07:29,850 --> 00:07:31,480
It's written all over your face.

102
00:07:37,990 --> 00:07:39,150
Bro.

103
00:07:39,530 --> 00:07:41,790
Would you ever keep a
secret from your friends?

104
00:07:42,970 --> 00:07:43,970
Hmm...

105
00:07:45,630 --> 00:07:50,370
Well, if telling them
might ruin our relationship,

106
00:07:50,570 --> 00:07:52,470
then I'd probably keep it a secret.

107
00:07:54,900 --> 00:07:55,940
But,

108
00:07:57,887 --> 00:08:00,556
if it's a friend I feel
I can absolutely trust,

109
00:08:00,580 --> 00:08:01,780
I'd tell them everything.

110
00:08:02,140 --> 00:08:03,550
Because I trust them.

111
00:08:05,780 --> 00:08:06,920
What about you, Hare?

112
00:08:10,550 --> 00:08:12,890
I really want to tell them.

113
00:08:14,920 --> 00:08:17,890
In that case, shouldn't
you just cherish that feeling?

114
00:08:24,500 --> 00:08:27,370
Though I don't know
if it'll actually be completely fine.

115
00:08:27,640 --> 00:08:28,640
Yeah.

116
00:08:31,570 --> 00:08:32,980
- Eat up.
- Yeah.

117
00:08:36,950 --> 00:08:37,950
Is it good?

118
00:08:38,970 --> 00:08:39,970
Yeah.

119
00:08:40,880 --> 00:08:43,289
I blended the spices
from scratch, you know.

120
00:08:43,290 --> 00:08:44,720
Whoa, seriously?

121
00:08:53,530 --> 00:08:54,530
Mayama.

122
00:08:55,170 --> 00:08:56,570
Try this.

123
00:08:57,130 --> 00:08:58,130
Right now.

124
00:08:58,470 --> 00:08:59,510
- Just take a bite.
- Okay.

125
00:08:59,710 --> 00:09:00,870
Tell me what you think.

126
00:09:01,830 --> 00:09:03,530
- Okay.
- Hurry, eat it.

127
00:09:03,550 --> 00:09:04,550
Okay.

128
00:09:04,610 --> 00:09:05,610
Hurry up and try it.

129
00:09:06,140 --> 00:09:07,420
- Thanks for the food.
- Alright.

130
00:09:07,970 --> 00:09:08,970
How is it?

131
00:09:13,620 --> 00:09:14,620
Huh?

132
00:09:23,550 --> 00:09:24,590
Sorry to keep you waiting.

133
00:09:28,950 --> 00:09:33,340
Everything started on that day.

134
00:09:34,100 --> 00:09:37,300
(I like you.)

135
00:10:00,030 --> 00:10:01,160
You're early today.

136
00:10:01,970 --> 00:10:02,970
Yeah.

137
00:10:03,570 --> 00:10:04,570
Shall we go?

138
00:10:23,030 --> 00:10:24,920
About what we talked about last time.

139
00:10:28,190 --> 00:10:29,190
Yeah.

140
00:10:32,090 --> 00:10:34,330
I really do want to tell the two of them.

141
00:10:40,010 --> 00:10:43,010
I'm really happy that
you're worried about me.

142
00:10:45,350 --> 00:10:46,350
But...

143
00:10:49,770 --> 00:10:51,150
The principal's bread.

144
00:10:51,890 --> 00:10:53,330
It got better.

145
00:10:55,480 --> 00:10:56,480
Huh?

146
00:10:57,190 --> 00:10:59,560
I heard he spent the
whole summer improving it.

147
00:11:01,660 --> 00:11:04,990
People change as time goes by.

148
00:11:06,460 --> 00:11:08,700
That's just a matter of course.

149
00:11:10,250 --> 00:11:13,840
But I think it's weird
to hide something so natural.

150
00:11:16,990 --> 00:11:19,990
Of course, if you're really uneasy
about it, then we shouldn't say anything.

151
00:11:22,850 --> 00:11:24,210
But I...

152
00:11:28,210 --> 00:11:30,950
Whether it's the time I
spend alone with you like this,

153
00:11:32,420 --> 00:11:35,390
or the time the four of us spend together
with Sakaki and Tsunekawada,

154
00:11:37,050 --> 00:11:38,370
I love it all.

155
00:11:40,630 --> 00:11:42,660
So I don't want to hide anything.

156
00:11:48,000 --> 00:11:49,140
I understand.

157
00:11:51,370 --> 00:11:53,080
If you say so.

158
00:11:54,340 --> 00:11:57,810
Actually, I really want
to show off to them too.

159
00:12:10,810 --> 00:12:11,810
It's really good.

160
00:12:12,690 --> 00:12:13,700
Then I'll have some too.

161
00:12:18,250 --> 00:12:19,290
Sorry to keep you waiting.

162
00:12:19,740 --> 00:12:21,170
Why did you call us here?

163
00:12:24,140 --> 00:12:26,580
There's something we
want to tell you today.

164
00:12:26,950 --> 00:12:28,859
What, did Sakaki mess up again?

165
00:12:28,860 --> 00:12:30,110
I didn't do anything, okay?

166
00:12:30,630 --> 00:12:31,630
I didn't mess up, did I?

167
00:12:32,410 --> 00:12:33,410
Um...

168
00:12:33,720 --> 00:12:37,296
Is it about how I secretly took one of Mayama's
mechanical pencil leads without telling him?

169
00:12:37,320 --> 00:12:38,760
I'm just finding out about this now.

170
00:12:39,390 --> 00:12:42,160
Then is it about how I took
a bite of Asamiya's bread?

171
00:12:42,190 --> 00:12:43,430
It's not that either.

172
00:12:43,930 --> 00:12:46,499
If we let him keep talking,
he's just gonna spill more secrets.

173
00:12:46,500 --> 00:12:47,290
Then...

174
00:12:47,291 --> 00:12:48,430
Let's hear them out first.

175
00:12:51,330 --> 00:12:52,500
Um.

176
00:12:54,300 --> 00:12:55,670
Well...

177
00:12:57,070 --> 00:12:58,340
I'll say it.

178
00:12:58,410 --> 00:12:59,540
No need.

179
00:13:06,950 --> 00:13:09,920
We're dating.

180
00:13:11,850 --> 00:13:12,850
Eh...

181
00:13:13,690 --> 00:13:17,430
We started dating on the day Sakaki
took me to that mixer at the karaoke place.

182
00:13:18,790 --> 00:13:21,430
We didn't want to keep
it a secret from you guys.

183
00:13:23,830 --> 00:13:25,400
You're surprised, right?

184
00:13:28,640 --> 00:13:30,710
More like...

185
00:13:32,740 --> 00:13:34,180
It was actually super obvious.

186
00:13:35,990 --> 00:13:36,990
Huh?

187
00:13:37,670 --> 00:13:41,380
First of all, it was super
obvious that Asamiya liked you.

188
00:13:41,780 --> 00:13:44,190
And the distance between you and Asamiya

189
00:13:44,350 --> 00:13:46,460
is completely different
from the first semester.

190
00:13:47,120 --> 00:13:48,460
Was it that obvious?

191
00:13:49,270 --> 00:13:53,200
I thought you guys dating
was just an unspoken agreement among us.

192
00:13:53,360 --> 00:13:57,470
It's actually more shocking that you
thought you were hiding it so well.

193
00:13:58,290 --> 00:13:59,290
Right?

194
00:14:02,590 --> 00:14:03,590
Sakaki?

195
00:14:05,740 --> 00:14:07,710
I had no idea.

196
00:14:08,610 --> 00:14:09,980
Eh...

197
00:14:11,010 --> 00:14:12,280
You guys are dating?

198
00:14:12,410 --> 00:14:13,580
Seriously?

199
00:14:14,190 --> 00:14:15,190
Yeah.

200
00:14:18,330 --> 00:14:19,330
I object.

201
00:14:21,260 --> 00:14:22,520
I mean, it's true.

202
00:14:23,030 --> 00:14:24,536
It's totally unfair that it's just you two.

203
00:14:24,560 --> 00:14:26,530
What about me?
What about my love life?

204
00:14:27,550 --> 00:14:28,830
What are you even talking about?

205
00:14:30,900 --> 00:14:33,570
But even if you guys are dating,

206
00:14:34,070 --> 00:14:36,640
we're still the same as before.
Nothing's going to change.

207
00:14:37,140 --> 00:14:38,740
Asamiya is still Asamiya.

208
00:14:39,070 --> 00:14:40,430
And Mayama is still Mayama, right?

209
00:14:41,410 --> 00:14:42,410
Yeah.

210
00:14:42,810 --> 00:14:44,510
Nothing's going to change.

211
00:14:47,450 --> 00:14:49,480
But hey,

212
00:14:51,490 --> 00:14:53,360
thanks for being honest with us.

213
00:14:54,270 --> 00:14:55,270
Yeah.

214
00:14:56,390 --> 00:14:57,260
Sakaki?

215
00:14:57,261 --> 00:14:58,769
I wish you guys the best.

216
00:14:58,770 --> 00:15:00,430
Man, I'm so freaking jealous!

217
00:15:02,430 --> 00:15:03,550
Come on, don't be like that.

218
00:15:05,730 --> 00:15:07,300
Hey, hey, hey, hey!

219
00:15:08,130 --> 00:15:10,010
Sorry, sorry, sorry!

220
00:15:11,770 --> 00:15:13,190
It's cold! So cold!

221
00:15:13,350 --> 00:15:14,780
My bad, my bad!

222
00:15:34,630 --> 00:15:36,370
Sorry, sorry!

223
00:15:37,200 --> 00:15:39,330
It's freezing! So cold!

224
00:15:46,170 --> 00:15:49,240
It's been almost a month since
the second semester started.

225
00:15:49,280 --> 00:15:51,809
I heard Teacher Komori got married.

226
00:15:51,810 --> 00:15:53,580
No wonder she's been a bit nicer lately.

227
00:15:54,920 --> 00:15:56,390
People really do change.

228
00:15:56,920 --> 00:15:57,920
Yeah.

229
00:15:58,350 --> 00:16:02,260
Anyway,
we're going to change seats now.

230
00:16:06,050 --> 00:16:07,560
Change seats?

231
00:16:12,490 --> 00:16:13,490
Teacher.

232
00:16:14,500 --> 00:16:15,500
What is it?

233
00:16:17,310 --> 00:16:18,770
I object to changing seats.

234
00:16:19,340 --> 00:16:20,410
Objection overruled.

235
00:16:22,740 --> 00:16:24,850
- Darn it.
- Of course she'd say no.

236
00:16:26,350 --> 00:16:30,620
Let's start with this row.
Come up and draw lots in order.

237
00:16:31,520 --> 00:16:33,389
Fate is just too cruel.

238
00:16:33,390 --> 00:16:35,660
Nah, you're exaggerating.

239
00:16:36,230 --> 00:16:38,030
Actually, maybe it's not an exaggeration...

240
00:17:04,190 --> 00:17:05,550
Are you serious?

241
00:17:08,020 --> 00:17:11,460
I wouldn't even mind using up
all my life's luck right here.

242
00:17:21,140 --> 00:17:23,110
Thank goodness we weren't separated.

243
00:17:24,370 --> 00:17:27,840
Though it's a bummer
I can't admire your back anymore.

244
00:17:29,050 --> 00:17:31,050
All right, quiet down.

245
00:17:31,750 --> 00:17:35,280
Please pass the parent-teacher
conference forms forward from the back.

246
00:18:20,100 --> 00:18:24,700
(I like Asamiya.)

247
00:18:35,420 --> 00:18:37,359
Sakaki and the others
said they headed home first.

248
00:18:37,360 --> 00:18:38,360
I see.

249
00:18:38,910 --> 00:18:40,910
Do you think they're trying
to give us some space?

250
00:18:41,020 --> 00:18:42,596
It's fine. It's nice to
have this once in a while.

251
00:18:42,620 --> 00:18:44,660
They're usually so bad at
reading the room, anyway.

252
00:18:47,090 --> 00:18:48,090
Thank you.

253
00:18:49,740 --> 00:18:50,740
Huh?

254
00:18:50,920 --> 00:18:52,830
Because I never really said it properly.

255
00:18:54,580 --> 00:18:56,780
I'm really glad we came
clean to Sakaki and the others.

256
00:19:00,370 --> 00:19:01,370
Yeah.

257
00:19:03,110 --> 00:19:04,110
It's just...

258
00:19:06,060 --> 00:19:07,060
Just what?

259
00:19:08,060 --> 00:19:12,580
I feel like the restraints on my heart
have been taken off.

260
00:19:18,900 --> 00:19:22,519
If you could see
what's going on in my head right now,

261
00:19:22,520 --> 00:19:24,030
you'd probably run for the hills.

262
00:19:27,960 --> 00:19:30,000
What are you thinking about?

263
00:19:31,420 --> 00:19:32,430
Can I really say it?

264
00:19:33,540 --> 00:19:34,540
Huh?

265
00:19:36,940 --> 00:19:43,450
If I can tell you
what I want to do to you, Mayama...

266
00:19:48,350 --> 00:19:52,890
and if I can actually act on all of it,
then I'll tell you.

267
00:19:55,620 --> 00:19:56,620
For example...

268
00:19:58,640 --> 00:20:00,460
Like wanting to bite you right here.

269
00:20:07,500 --> 00:20:11,440
Or slipping my hand
under this shirt.

270
00:20:16,220 --> 00:20:20,320
But if I do something like that even once,

271
00:20:21,420 --> 00:20:23,490
I don't think I'd be able to stop.

272
00:20:27,760 --> 00:20:28,920
Um...

273
00:20:34,800 --> 00:20:36,870
You're not the only one.

274
00:20:41,300 --> 00:20:49,300
I want to do those things with you, too.

275
00:21:14,320 --> 00:21:15,800
Let's stop here for today.

276
00:21:22,480 --> 00:21:23,810
Someone might come.

277
00:21:26,320 --> 00:21:29,520
We'll cross that bridge if
someone actually comes.

278
00:21:58,840 --> 00:22:03,190
My romance with Asamiya,
which started after moving seats.

279
00:22:06,000 --> 00:22:08,420
We'll definitely change
seats again in the future.

280
00:22:09,220 --> 00:22:14,860
People and seasons will
also change, little by little.

281
00:22:16,820 --> 00:22:18,070
But...

282
00:22:20,420 --> 00:22:21,420
Isn't it about time...

283
00:22:22,580 --> 00:22:23,270
Hmm?

284
00:22:23,271 --> 00:22:25,431
Should we start calling
each other by our first names?

285
00:22:26,180 --> 00:22:27,180
Huh?

286
00:22:28,140 --> 00:22:29,140
Is that a no?

287
00:22:29,570 --> 00:22:30,570
No.

288
00:22:31,210 --> 00:22:33,480
It's just that Asamiya is... Asamiya.

289
00:22:34,150 --> 00:22:35,926
I guess you could say
I'm a bit shy about it.

290
00:22:35,950 --> 00:22:37,890
What does it matter, Hare?

291
00:22:46,720 --> 00:22:48,000
Kousei.

292
00:22:50,230 --> 00:22:51,430
I can't hear you.

293
00:22:57,740 --> 00:22:58,870
Kousei.

294
00:23:02,180 --> 00:23:03,580
Good job.

295
00:23:04,250 --> 00:23:05,780
Geez.

296
00:23:07,740 --> 00:23:08,740
Let's go.

297
00:23:19,420 --> 00:23:20,420
That day.

298
00:23:21,940 --> 00:23:25,100
Only this romance,
which started from that one seat change,

299
00:23:27,720 --> 00:23:32,720
will surely continue
unchanged from now on.
